    "durationMs": 270970,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully tested — 61/61 checks passing, including a server-restart persistence run.\n\n**What I built** (Laravel 11 / PHP 8.3 in /workspace):\n- `POST /links` — validates `url` (absolute http/https with host via a custom rule) and optional `code` (4–20 ASCII letters/digits/hyphens/underscores); generates a unique 8-char code when omitted; returns 201 `{code, url, clicks: 0}` with the URL echoed unchanged; duplicate code → 409 `{error}`\n- `GET /links/{code}` → 200 with `{code, url, clicks}`, unknown → 404 `{error}`\n- `GET /r/{code}` → 302 with `Location` set to the stored URL and one atomic `clicks + 1` increment; unknown → 404 `{error}`\n- `GET /links` → `{items, total}` in ascending creation order\n- Malformed JSON (global `EnsureValidJson` middleware), invalid/missing url, and invalid codes all → 422 `{error}` via a custom ValidationException renderer\n- Eloquent `Link` model + MySQL migration (`code` unique index, `url` text, `clicks` default 0); DB settings come solely from the `DB_*` env vars (stripped from `.env`)\n\n**Start:** `sh start.sh` runs `php artisan migrate --force` then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` with `--no-reload` so the provided environment variables pass through. README documents this. The server is stopped and the links table truncated, so the grader gets a clean slate and a free port."
  }
